#!/bin/zsh
# usage: codex-analyze.sh <task-slug>   (analysis phase after the coordinator ran exp/<slug>/spec.json)
S="${CODEX_LOGS:-$HOME/.cache/unsw-codex}"; mkdir -p "$S"
R="~/01. Project/개인 프로젝트/unsw-swarm"
echo "$(date +%H:%M:%S) start analyze $1" >> $S/codex-build-runner.log
cd "$R" && nice -n 10 codex exec -m gpt-6.1-sol -c 'model_reasoning_effort="high"' -C "$R" -s workspace-write --skip-git-repo-check -o $S/codex-analyze-$1-last.txt "ANALYSIS phase for v1.8 work item '$1'. The coordinator has run exp/$1/spec.json (games and the run log are under exp/$1/). Read AGENTS.md section 4 (mechanism criteria only, no win-count gates), the item's pre-registration in versions/v1.8/VERSION.md and exp/$1/ANALYZE.md. Run the analysis exactly as ANALYZE.md says (replay tools with UNSW_RULES=123). Report every pre-registered criterion with value, N and pass/fail, plus 2 board pictures of the intended situation (exp/v16/board.js or eval/board.js). Append the results as a new section of versions/v1.8/VERSION.md, with the real time from date, and write exp/$1/RESULT.txt (8 lines). The last line is the proposal: switch ON or OFF by the partial-application rule (purpose moved the intended way and nothing broke means ON). 'Nothing broke' = identity, CPU, errors, and no harm at the decisions the switch changed (same input: new choice survives; old choice would die; no new death within a few rounds caused by the new choice). After the first changed decision on/off games diverge: report raw death counts and per-key queen lifetimes in BOTH directions as context only, never as a gate; never gate on a measure that only the on arm can produce. The harm gate is tools/firstdiv.js on the on/off sets (exp/firstdiv/RESULT.md shows usage): pass when, at k=3 for the changed dragon and k=50 for the queen, harm <= help, with a board and one-line cause for every harm case (feeding deaths marked as intended). Do not edit the bot or params, do not run games, do not commit, no network. Keep it short." < /dev/null > $S/codex-analyze-$1.log 2>&1
echo "$(date +%H:%M:%S) exit $? analyze $1" >> $S/codex-build-runner.log
